  "description": "California's 35th Congressional District, located in the Inland Empire and parts of eastern Los Angeles County and western San Bernardino County, is holding a general election on November 3, 2026. Incumbent Democrat Norma Torres, first elected in 2014, faces Republican challenger Mike Cargile in a rematch of their 2020, 2022, and 2024 contests. The district has been reliably Democratic — Torres won with over 65% in previous cycles — and Cook Political Report rates the race as \"Solid Democratic.\" Key issues include immigration, border security, inflation, public safety, and abortion rights, with Torres emphasizing her record of delivering federal funding for the district and Cargile campaigning as an America First conservative.",
