      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Norma Torres is the incumbent U.S. Representative for California's 35th Congressional District, first elected in 2014. Born in Guatemala and raised in Southern California, she previously served as Mayor of Pomona, in the California State Assembly, and in the California State Senate. Torres sits on the House Appropriations Committee and the Committee on House Administration, and she focuses on issues including labor rights, immigration reform, and federal funding for the Inland Empire.",
